-- title:
--   u is a non-zero-divisor on W[[u,v]]/(uv-π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$ be an element belonging to the monoid of non-zero-divisors of $W$, i.e. such that $x\pi = 0$ forces $x = 0$. Form the ring `UVCrossingModel W π`, defined as the quotient of the ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)$ of formal power series in two variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ over $W$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, where $C$ is the constant-coefficient inclusion of $W$; thus the quotient is $W[[u,v]]/(uv - \pi)$ with $u = X_0$, $v = X_1$. The assertion is that the distinguished element `U π` of this quotient lies in the monoid of non-zero-divisors of `UVCrossingModel W π`: every $x$ in the quotient with $x \cdot U(\pi) = 0$ is zero. No hypothesis on $W$ beyond commutativity is imposed, and the only hypothesis on $\pi$ is that it be a non-zero-divisor in $W$.
--
--   This records the basic regularity property of the branch coordinate on the standard model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ of a crossing; for $W$ the Witt vectors of $\bar{\mathbb F}_p$ and $\pi = p$ this is the completed strict henselisation of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-moduli problem at a supersingular point, whose special fibre has an ordinary double point (so that for $\pi = 0$ the conclusion genuinely fails, $uv = 0$ with $v \neq 0$). It feeds the structural results on elements of the crossing model, such as the factorisations `exists_eq_unit_mul_U_pow_mul_pow_of_forall_height_eq_one_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul` and `exists_pow_eq_unit_mul_U_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_thicknessOne`.
